  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Cohesive dark technical art direction, disciplined cyan/red accents, strong headline, consistent cards, and credible responsive reflow. It falls short of demo-ready polish: mobile supporting text and chart labels are extremely small, the PR curve wastes much of its plotting area, the desktop hero has excessive empty space and a visually detached annotation, and the mobile header drops the brand name while exposing only an ambiguous “SWIPE” cue. Low-contrast microcopy and dense ablation content weaken hierarchy across smaller viewports; header contrast also remains unproven by the supplied audit.",
    "fix": "Raise mobile body/label sizes and contrast, simplify chart annotations, tighten the desktop hero composition, give the plots more purposeful scales, and redesign the small-screen header with persistent identity plus a clearer current-section/navigation affordance.",
